            {"id": "c", "text": "Software as a Service (SaaS)", "correct": True, "rationale": "Correct. SaaS delivers a fully managed, ready-to-use application to end users. The vendor handles the entire technology stack; the customer only manages user accounts, data, and configuration settings. A hosted email/calendar service accessed via browser is a textbook SaaS example."},
            {"id": "d", "text": "Desktop as a Service (DaaS)", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. DaaS delivers a full virtual desktop operating environment, not a specific hosted business application. The agency needs email and calendar, not a virtual Windows or Linux desktop."},
