            {"id": "c", "text": "Community cloud", "correct": True, "rationale": "Correct. A community cloud is shared infrastructure used exclusively by a group of organizations with common concerns — in this case, five banks sharing regulatory compliance requirements. Costs and governance are distributed among the members, and third-party hosting is permitted."},
            {"id": "d", "text": "Hybrid cloud", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. Hybrid cloud integrates two or more distinct cloud deployment models (typically private + public). This scenario describes a single shared environment serving a specific community, not a bridging of two different cloud types."},
