            {"id": "b", "text": "Test and development environment", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. A test/development environment is used to test software changes or new deployments before production release. The team is running the legacy CAD application in permanent production use, not testing a new version or change."},
            {"id": "c", "text": "Legacy software support", "correct": True, "rationale": "Correct. Legacy software support is the use case where a VM running an older OS (Windows XP in this case) is maintained specifically because required software cannot run on newer operating systems. Virtualizing the old OS preserves access to the legacy application without maintaining physical old hardware."},
            {"id": "d", "text": "Cloud-based virtual desktop", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. A cloud-based virtual desktop (DaaS) is hosted in a provider's cloud infrastructure. The scenario describes on-premises virtualization to run a legacy application, not provisioning virtual desktops from a cloud provider."},
